          "confidence": 0.92,
          "synopsis": "Demonstrates running an independent samples t-test in jamovi: grade is the dependent variable and tutor the grouping variable. Output reports the t-statistic, degrees of freedom, p-value, a confidence interval for the difference between group means, and an effect size. The example gives Anastasia's mean 74.53 and Bernadette's 69.06, difference 5.48, with 95% CI [0.20, 10.76], and shows a write-up: t(31) = 2.1, p < .05, CI95 = [0.2, 10.8], d = .74. Advises reporting effect size and confidence interval.",
          "pages": [
